---
interface Props {
  siteName: string;
  contactEmail: string;
}
const { siteName, contactEmail } = Astro.props;
---

<p class="lead">
  {siteName} is an NM Labs project. It helps spot Android TV box specs that are inconsistent with
  the hardware.
</p>

<h2>What the site does (and does not do)</h2>
<p>
  The site compares the advertised specs with the known hardware limits of the SoC and with cases
  already reported. It detects <strong>impossibilities</strong> and <strong>known cases</strong>. It
  never proves that a box is genuine: a "plausible" verdict only means that no impossibility was
  detected.
</p>

<h2>Method and status of the data</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Every technical value has a source and a status, "verified" or "unverified".</li>
  <li>
    <strong>Verified</strong>: a manufacturer datasheet or product page was read, or at least two
    independent sources (sites on different domains) give the same value. Only this data can produce
    an "impossible" verdict.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Single source</strong>: a single forum or article. The verdict stays at "suspect" at
    most.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Unsourced hypothesis</strong>: no conclusion is drawn from it.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Reported cases</h2>
<p>
  Cases are sourced observations summarised in our own words, never accusations. We do not name
  individual sellers. Brand and model names are used for identification only.
</p>

<h2 id="correction">Request a correction or removal</h2>
<p>
  If some information concerns you and seems inaccurate, write to
  <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. We reply quickly and correct or remove
  whatever needs to be.
</p>

<h2>Licences</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Code: MIT licence.</li>
  <li>
    Data (<code>data/</code> folder): CC BY 4.0 licence, with the attribution "tvbox-check / NM
    Labs".
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Privacy</h2>
<p>
  The site uses no cookie and shows no consent banner. It measures its traffic with Cloudflare Web
  Analytics: aggregated audience measurement, with no cookie and no persistent identifier, and not
  used for any advertising. The data you enter in the checker stays in your browser and is never
  sent. Comments, when displayed, only load on request and go through GitHub (giscus), which applies
  its own rules.
</p>
